org&gt; " fail_count="4" gerrit_number="335880" owner_email="domlaskowski@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/80/335880/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0fb8347e50941c95f60d3edb45fed5419ad7adf4" commit="f03a1e05863e242ad680dfce9ae5c27f477f006c" commit_message="finalize: make sure virtual dev is off before in-place wiping  For in-place wiping, we cut-off device immediately after wiping without additional reboot. However, crossystem disable_dev_request=1 requires reboot to save the flag into flash on some device. Immediately cut-off causes the flag corrupt and device will not leave dev mode.  This CL add a check. For factory process, finalize will fail if virtual dev is on. For RMA, reboot is used instead of cut-off.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:51846 TEST=Run finalize on Chell with virtual dev sw on/off.  Change-Id: I0fb8347e50941c95f60d3edb45fed5419ad7adf4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/336610 Commit-Ready: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="336610" owner_email="shunhsingou@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/10/336610/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I36940cb3b69adf9a9d894487965829a600b2ff97" commit="11fccbad4190e124f6c6dbf0c6dce07ad0de4bea" commit_message="chromeos-chrome/chromeos-chrome-9999.ebuild: remove use_vgem_map definition.  dma_buf mmap replaced vgem, so remove the stale definition.  BUG=chromium:581151 TEST=amd64-generic  Change-Id: I36940cb3b69adf9a9d894487965829a600b2ff97 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.g